    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d177">

                <pb facs="0259" n="191" xml:id="pg191"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72111/1396½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to President Wilson </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 9, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: I enclose a
                        statement<anchor n="29" xml:id="d177-f1"/> which, with your approval, I will
                    give out to the press, in regard to the demands made upon us to protest against
                    the invasion of Belgium by Germany. Mr. Lansing prepared a memorandum to which I
                    made some amendments and this statement is the result of our conference on the
                    subject. If you will return Mr. Lansing’s letter and this statement with such
                    corrections as you wish to make, I will give the statement out early next
                    week.</p>
                <p>With assurances [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d177-f1" n="29" xml:id="d177-f1-content">
